  "term": "fasciculus gracilis",
  "definition": "The fasciculus gracilis is a part of the spinal cord’s dorsal column made up of axons. In the source material, it is described as becoming demyelinated and later losing axons, especially in its core and then its surface, although remyelination can protect some sub-pial axons.",
